{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1404506-justifying-an-imp-familiar","id":1404506,"title":"Justifying an imp familiar?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-24T19:49:48-07:00","id":1404506,"title":"Justifying an imp familiar?","content":"So a Hermetic takes an imp for a familiar, as made optional by Forged by Dragon\u2019s Fire, except how does he justify it to his peers? Can you take something that is even superficially aligned with the Nephandi without risking major suspicion from other mages?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T20:28:50-07:00","id":1404513,"title":"","content":"Be a demonologist that bound it into service.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4017-angryicecream","name":"angryicecream","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T20:58:27-07:00","id":1404521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1404506-justifying-an-imp-familiar#post1404506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So a Hermetic takes an imp for a familiar, as made optional by Forged by Dragon\u2019s Fire, except how does he justify it to his peers? Can you take something that is even superficially aligned with the Nephandi without risking major suspicion from other mages?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is the Faustian pact, manifest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T23:52:00-07:00","id":1404533,"title":"","content":"Well, according to (of all things) Book Of The Fallen, at least in ye olde Mythic Age they seem to have been a bit more accepted. And these days can be...interesting.<br /> <br /> &quot;Throughout the Mythic Ages, imps were perhaps best known for their role as familiars among the ranks of witches and wizards. In that role, they\u2019ll still serve when need be \u2014 it is, after all, traditional. This egalitarian age, however, encourages imps to become literal free spirits, companions and perhaps even masters of mortals who lack the old methods of command and control. And so, although you\u2019ll still find imps darting to and fro around a mage\u2019s sanctuary, an imp\u2019s more likely to be watching porn or playing video games alongside his unAwakened buddy. After millennia of insults and servitude, these tiny demons enjoy whatever liberties they can grab.&quot;<br /> <br /> While Hermes officially does not condone summoning and binding demons into service (Read: Don't ask, don't tell), an Imp probably rides that blurry grey line of &quot;We absolutely do not approve of this! But if you keep the little guy in check...&quot;<br /> <br /> Plot Twist: Now, if it is a full fledged Demon *posing* as an Imp, things might get very very...complicated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 07-25-2020, 02:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T01:50:43-07:00","id":1404547,"title":"","content":"Are Imps really that bad?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.t